1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,091
Welcome to the Rosetta DBT Studio release roundup.

2
00:00:04,372 --> 00:00:15,102
In the last three weeks we shipped four releases: 1.6.82, 1.6.83, 1.7.0 and 1.7.1.

3
00:00:15,382 --> 00:00:24,513
Let’s walk through what’s new, from a brand-new home dashboard and Python notebooks to MySQL, Snowflake browser login, and images in the AI chat.

4
00:00:25,613 --> 00:00:26,850
Here’s the timeline.

5
00:00:27,130 --> 00:00:34,128
1.6.82 landed on September 17th with pipeline templates and setup improvements.

6
00:00:34,408 --> 00:00:40,829
1.6.83 followed on September 22nd with the dbt-Kinetica adapter.

7
00:00:41,109 --> 00:00:50,048
1.7.0, on September 29th, was the big one: a new dashboard, Python notebooks and Snowflake browser authentication.

8
00:00:50,327 --> 00:00:57,602
And 1.7.1, on October 2nd, added MySQL, a smarter schema tree and multimodal AI.

9
00:00:58,702 --> 00:01:03,545
Starting with 1.7.0, Studio opens on the new Workspace Overview.

10
00:01:03,825 --> 00:01:13,340
Every module is one click away: dbt Project, Notebook, SQL Editor, Analytics, Data Lake, Object Explorer, Pipeline and ETL.

11
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:21,726
Below them you’ll find your recent projects and configured connections, and the app navigation has been reorganized around these modules.

12
00:01:22,826 --> 00:01:24,426
Notebooks now run Python.

13
00:01:24,706 --> 00:01:30,616
Here, a SQL cell queries the connected DuckDB database and saves its result as df.

14
00:01:30,896 --> 00:01:39,642
The next Python cell picks it up as a pandas DataFrame and displays it in an interactive table with column types, row filtering and paging.

15
00:01:40,742 --> 00:01:42,641
The workflow has three cell types.

16
00:01:42,921 --> 00:01:48,425
SQL cells run against the selected connection, and Result as gives the output a name.

17
00:01:48,705 --> 00:01:51,478
Python cells use that name as a DataFrame.

18
00:01:51,758 --> 00:01:53,678
Text cells add headings and notes.

19
00:01:53,958 --> 00:02:00,273
Just run cells from top to bottom: a Python cell can only use df after its SQL cell has run.

20
00:02:00,553 --> 00:02:04,862
The toolbar shows the Python version and whether the kernel is idle or busy.

21
00:02:05,962 --> 00:02:09,696
Snowflake connections can now sign in through your web browser.

22
00:02:09,976 --> 00:02:17,890
Choose Web Browser instead of Password Login, fill in your account, warehouse, role, database and schema, and click Test Connection.

23
00:02:18,170 --> 00:02:25,445
Studio opens Snowflake’s login page; finish there and you’re authenticated, without typing a password into Studio.

24
00:02:25,725 --> 00:02:27,773
You can revoke the token at any time.

25
00:02:28,873 --> 00:02:32,969
1.7.0 also removes some everyday interruptions.

26
00:02:33,249 --> 00:02:39,372
The SQL editor no longer crashes when a database returns an error object instead of a message.

27
00:02:39,652 --> 00:02:44,323
Unreachable servers no longer trigger repeated Failed to fetch schema alerts.

28
00:02:44,603 --> 00:02:50,513
And picking a project from its card or from the top-bar dropdown now takes you straight into that project.

29
00:02:51,613 --> 00:02:54,642
Release 1.7.1 adds MySQL.

30
00:02:54,922 --> 00:03:06,399
Create a connection with host, port, database, schema, username and password, turn on SSL or TLS if your server needs it, and test the connection before you save.

31
00:03:07,499 --> 00:03:11,958
Once connected, MySQL works in the SQL editor like any other source.

32
00:03:12,238 --> 00:03:17,849
Browse databases and tables in the schema tree, and run queries or DDL statements.

33
00:03:18,129 --> 00:03:26,534
The same release adds dbt-compatibility indicators, so you can see at a glance which connection types work with a dbt project.

34
00:03:27,634 --> 00:03:32,498
The schema tree now has a context menu, in both the SQL editor and notebooks.

35
00:03:32,778 --> 00:03:37,727
Right-click a table to insert or copy its name, qualified name or column list.

36
00:03:38,007 --> 00:03:42,317
Generate SELECT star, SELECT columns, COUNT or an INSERT template.

37
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:45,839
Preview the data, rename the table, or refresh the schema.

38
00:03:46,119 --> 00:03:49,447
You can also drag items from the tree straight into your editor.

39
00:03:50,547 --> 00:03:53,321
The Rosetta AI agent is now multimodal.

40
00:03:53,601 --> 00:04:00,129
Attach a screenshot, a diagram or an error dialog to your chat message, preview it full size, and send it.

41
00:04:00,409 --> 00:04:05,913
The agent uses the image together with your project, selected files and the conversation.

42
00:04:06,193 --> 00:04:08,689
Just pick a model that supports image input.

43
00:04:09,789 --> 00:04:12,583
1.7.1 also brings fixes.

44
00:04:12,863 --> 00:04:17,322
The local SQLite catalog for Apache Iceberg now works on Windows.

45
00:04:17,602 --> 00:04:22,978
The AI icon in the header renders correctly, and an environment variable issue is fixed.

46
00:04:23,258 --> 00:04:30,661
And Playwright for the testing tool now ships inside the image, so it no longer has to be downloaded and installed separately.

47
00:04:31,761 --> 00:04:36,476
Back in 1.6.83 we added the dbt-Kinetica adapter.

48
00:04:36,756 --> 00:04:40,766
You’ll find it under Settings, dbt Core, Adapter packages.

49
00:04:41,046 --> 00:04:52,844
It isn’t published on PyPI, so Studio installs it directly from the rosettadb kinetica-dbt-adapter repository on GitHub, and Update from source pulls new versions.

50
00:04:53,123 --> 00:04:56,131
It requires dbt Core 1.8 or newer.

51
00:04:57,232 --> 00:05:00,154
And 1.6.82 laid the groundwork.

52
00:05:00,434 --> 00:05:03,869
Pipeline Templates can start from a ZIP project template.

53
00:05:04,149 --> 00:05:07,967
The Setup Wizard now includes a Local Runner installation step.

54
00:05:08,248 --> 00:05:12,962
Duplicate project detection is smarter, and project deletion errors are handled.

55
00:05:13,242 --> 00:05:18,874
The Studio database store was refactored, and DuckLake connections now show the right icon.

56
00:05:19,974 --> 00:05:24,966
That’s the roundup for 1.6.82 through 1.7.1.

57
00:05:25,246 --> 00:05:33,545
Download Rosetta DBT Studio from rosettadb.io, star the project on GitHub, and tell us what you’d like to see next.

58
00:05:33,825 --> 00:05:35,062
Thanks for watching.
